    "summary": "The command handlers use operation.effect and forward execution options, but several migrated projections and compatibility behaviors regress: summary volume is always zero, measurement updates no longer preserve the prior merged output, routine/user response envelopes change, and operation-domain failures are reported as generic usage failures.",
    "issues": [
      {
        "file": "/root/hevy-mcp-effect-ops-layer/packages/cli/src/commands/index.ts",
        "line": 701,
        "severity": "blocking",
        "description": "summary always emits total_volume_kg: 0. The migrated trainingSummary operation result has no total_volume_kg field (packages/operations/src/workflows.ts:78-89, 470-487), so this safeParse can never succeed. The previous CLI calculated volume from workout sets, and the public SummaryResult still requires this field; a real summary therefore silently loses a documented result."
      },
      {
        "file": "/root/hevy-mcp-effect-ops-layer/packages/cli/src/commands/index.ts",
        "line": 636,
        "severity": "blocking",
        "description": "measurements update now calls bodyMeasurements.update and reconstructs output only from the patch at lines 642-642. The previous command fetched the existing measurement, merged non-null changes, returned the complete merged measurement, and rejected an invalid/mismatched existing record. The new operations update returns only the date (packages/operations/src/body-measurements.ts:254-274), so partial updates change stdout and no longer preserve the established output behavior."
      },
      {
        "file": "/root/hevy-mcp-effect-ops-layer/packages/cli/src/commands/index.ts",
        "line": 359,
        "severity": "blocking",
        "description": "routine get and user now project normalized operation domain values rather than preserving the public CLI response envelopes. routines.get returns response.routine from the operations layer (packages/operations/src/routines.ts:417-423), while the old CLI wrapped the public getRoutineById response, whose API type is { routine?: Routine }; user.get similarly returns response.data (packages/operations/src/user.ts:38-44) while the old CLI wrapped the full UserInfoResponse. The handlers at lines 365-370 and 734-741 therefore change JSON/human output for real clients, even though the feature requires output compatibility."
      },
      {
        "file": "/root/hevy-mcp-effect-ops-layer/packages/cli/src/commands/index.ts",
        "line": 511,
        "severity": "blocking",
        "description": "exercises search no longer honors --max-pages as a scan limit. It invokes templates.listAll with no limit, which eagerly scans every page, then slices the already-fetched array at maxPages * 100 (lines 517-523). The old command stopped issuing requests once max-pages was reached and reported the capped pages_scanned value. This is observable network behavior and makes the preserved flag misleading."
      },
      {
        "file": "/root/hevy-mcp-effect-ops-layer/packages/cli/src/errors.ts",
        "line": 99,
        "severity": "blocking",
        "description": "The diagnostic classifier recognizes only client tagged errors (lines 27-43). Operations now fail with PaginationMismatchError, TrainingSummaryValidationError, WorkoutPrivacyError, WorkoutPayloadError, or EmptyMeasurementUpdateError, none of which are ApiResponseError or client tags, so runCli falls through to code 2 and the generic 'Command failed' message. In particular, API pagination failures from migrated list/events commands no longer classify as the required API failure (exit 3), and domain validation messages are lost."
      }
    ]
  },
